DATA LICENSE NOTE — SEPARATE FROM CODE

The data files under public/data/ are DERIVED WORKS of CC BY-SA licensed
sources and remain under their respective ShareAlike terms, independent of
the code dual-license above. In particular:

  - public/data/morph/  — derived from Morpheus analyses (CC BY-SA 3.0 US)
  - public/data/gloss/  — derived from LSJ via Perseus + Logeion
                          (CC BY-SA 3.0 US / CC BY-SA 4.0)
  - public/data/texts/  — classical corpus via PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit
                          (CC BY-SA 3.0) and Septuagint/Philo via
                          OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  - public/data/trans/  — classical translations are public domain except
                          where an upstream TEI header states otherwise
  - public/data/dicts/  — Autenrieth, A Homeric Dictionary (Harper &
                          Brothers, 1891): public domain; digitised text
                          courtesy of the Perseus Digital Library

See README.md § Sources & Licenses and src/about.ts for full citations.
Data is not covered by MIT/Apache; you must comply with CC BY-SA
ShareAlike when redistributing data shards.

