THIRD-PARTY RUNTIME DEPENDENCY NOTE

Build/runtime dependencies are permissively compatible with MIT OR
Apache-2.0 and do not change the code license:

  - vite (MIT), typescript (Apache-2.0), esbuild (MIT), rollup (MIT),
    postcss (MIT), playwright-core (Apache-2.0)

The optional offline TTS runtime espeak-ng (npm: espeak-ng, GPL-3.0-or-later)
is dynamically loaded as a WASM artifact (public/espeak-ng.wasm, not
committed; fetched/bundled via vite.config.ts). It is a separate
program under GPL-3.0 and is NOT covered by the MIT/Apache dual license;
if you distribute the WASM you must comply with GPL-3.0 for that artifact
alone. The rest of the codebase remains MIT OR Apache-2.0.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA NOTES (not covered by the code license above)

- Cunliffe, R.J., "A Lexicon of the Homeric Dialect" (Blackie/Toronto, 1924).
  Published before 1930; believed public domain (no renewal found; author
  d. 1956). Machine-readable TEI digitization by Gregory Crane
  (github.com/gregorycrane/Homerica); ingested to public/data/dicts/cunliffe/.
- Autenrieth, G., "A Homeric Dictionary" digitation, ingested to
  public/data/dicts/homer/ — same open-republication basis.
- Texts/morphology/translations retain their source licenses as documented in
  DEPLOYMENT.md / catalog.json entries and About page.
